35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The road closures didn’t stop community halls, but supplier delays are a real risk. We need to avoid dependencies on unreliable external partners.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that’s a huge relief! The halls stayed open, so we aren’t completely cut off. But losing the bus means an hour’s trip for many.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the grant only covers twelve months. After that, the flat budget absorbs the cost. That is a structural trap, not a temporary gap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@George, the old digitisation project failed, but the partner groups thrived. We have proof that community-led models work here.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, I found a gap. No one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators. We need to fix this before adding new duties.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
